Spec: HandlebarsHandler

Purpose:
  Own the Vynil-layer Handlebars engine: the @HandleBars newtype over
    @vynil_core::hbs::HandleBars that registers the nine Vynil contextual helpers
    (context selectors/labels, CRD and published-service probes, script-built image
    references and k8s resources maps, and the nested `render_template` /
    `render_file` recursion helpers) on top of the generic core surface, hands the
    engine to package scripts through @handlebars_rhai_register (`new_hbs` and its
    methods), freezes the native-helper name list via @VYNIL_HBS_HELPERS and
    @is_native_hbs_helper, and re-exports @Value plus the Handlebars template AST
    types for external template inspection.

Owns:
  ./handlebarshandler.rs

References:
  ./rhaihandler.rs — sole in-crate caller of @handlebars_rhai_register
    (@crate::rhaihandler::Script::new_core adds it; the @tests module here drives
    @crate::rhaihandler::Script::new under @cfg(test), product code depends on
    nothing in that module).
  ./tools.sdd, ./yamlhandler.sdd, ./instance_macros.sdd — approved calibration references.

Must:
  @HandleBars::new builds the complete engine as @vynil_core::hbs::HandleBars::new()
    (which is `handlebars_misc_helpers::new_hbs` plus the core vendored JSON helpers)
    then registers on @vynil_core::hbs::HandleBars::engine_mut exactly seven macro
    helpers under registered names `selector_from_ctx`→@selector,
    `labels_from_ctx`→@labels, `ctx_have_crd`→@have_crd,
    `have_system_service`→@have_system_service, `have_tenant_service`→@have_tenant_service,
    `render_template`→@render_template, `render_file`→@render_file, plus two Rhai
    script helpers `image_from_ctx` and `resources_from_ctx`; nothing else is added.
  The two @vynil_core::hbs::HandleBars::engine_mut script registrations go through
    @handlebars::Handlebars::register_script_helper, which compiles the Rhai source
    eagerly, and their @Result::Ok(()) is discarded with `let _` — a compile failure
    would silently leave the helper absent. In the locked build both scripts compile
    and behave as specified below (verified against a pinned 6.4.2/0.7.7/1.25.1 probe).
  Error texts of helper argument failures name the macro struct, not the registered
    name: `@selector`, `@labels` and `@have_crd` appear in messages while templates
    call them `selector_from_ctx`, `labels_from_ctx`, `ctx_have_crd`; `@have_system_service`,
    `@have_tenant_service`, `@render_template`, `@render_file` match their registered names.
  The engine inherits two engine-wide settings installed by the locked
    `handlebars_misc_helpers` `0.17.0` `setup_handlebars` inside the core constructor,
    attributed to that build: @handlebars::Handlebars::set_strict_mode(`true`) — an
    undefined variable reaching a strictly-typed helper parameter is a render error,
    not an empty value — and @handlebars::Handlebars::register_escape_fn with
    @handlebars::no_escape, replacing the `&"<>` @handlebars::html_escape default, so
    no `{{ }}` output is HTML-escaped anywhere (probed: `&`/`%26` from `url_encode`
    and `=` from base64 survive; json helper output carries raw quotes).
  Objects returned by helpers render through the locked handlebars @JsonRender::render
    placeholder — `{{selector_from_ctx this}}` prints the literal `[object]`, a null
    value prints the empty string — so @selector, @labels and `resources_from_ctx`
    results are only consumable via @JsonRender-free paths: subexpressions such as
    `json_to_str (resources_from_ctx this "app")`, block helpers such as
    `{{#each (selector_from_ctx this)}}`, or Rhai scripts reading the parameters.
  @selector (`selector_from_ctx`) takes @ctx: @Value (any JSON — object, string,
    null all accepted) plus optional hash `comp`: @str default `""`; returns the
    cloned object found at `ctx.instance.selector` when that is an object, else the
    empty object; a non-empty `comp` maps-inserts the key `app.kubernetes.io/component`
    after the copied entries — an equal existing key keeps its position and takes the
    `comp` value — while an empty `comp` (explicit or default) inserts nothing.
    `ctx` being absent (or an undefined variable under strict mode) fails rendering
    with `Helper/Decorator selector param with name ctx required but not found`.
  @labels (`labels_from_ctx`) is identical over `ctx.instance.labels`.
  @have_crd (`ctx_have_crd`) takes @ctx: @Value and a required `name`: @String — JSON
    numbers, bools and objects never satisfy the @String coercion and fail with
    `type mismatch for String` — and answers whether `ctx.cluster.crds` is an array
    containing a JSON string exactly equal to `name`; a missing or non-array `crds`
    is `false`, and non-string entries simply never match.
  @have_system_service and @have_tenant_service share the shape (required @ctx +
    @String `name`, @bool answer) over `ctx.cluster.services` and `ctx.tenant.services`
    respectively: true if some array element is an object whose `key` field equals
    `name` as a JSON string; non-object elements are inert, missing or non-array
    context answers `false`.
  `image_from_ctx` is an unguarded Rhai script on `params`: `params[0]` and
    `params[1]` are indexed raw — with fewer than two parameters the render fails with
    the handlebars-prefixed Rhai text `Cannot convert data to Rhai dynamic:` carrying an
    `Array index <n> out of bounds` — and it indexes
    `root["instance"]["images"][name]` with no type or presence guard, so a
    non-object `root` or an unknown `name` aborts mid-script (unknown name surfaces
    later as `Function not found: contains` against the unit image entry, at script
    line 3 position 21). The tag is `im["tag"]` only when the key exists and its
    value is not the unit `()` — a present `tag: null` therefore falls back — and the
    fallback `root["instance"]["package"]["app_version"]` is itself unguarded, so a
    missing package fails with `Indexer unavailable: () [string] (line 3, position 92)`.
    Success renders the Rhai template string `<registry>/<repository>:<tag>`.
  `resources_from_ctx` is the null-safe twin: every access chains with the Rhai
    optional-index `?` (`params[0]?["instance"]?["resources"]`, `root?[name]?...`) so
    any missing level yields the unit `()` and the helper returns an empty `#{}` map,
    not an error; `#{}` is the Rhai empty-map literal inside the plain Rust string
    (no Rust interpolation happens). It copies only the four leaf values
    `requests.cpu`, `requests.memory`, `limits.cpu`, `limits.memory` with their JSON
    types intact, adds the `requests` / `limits` parent keys only when at least one
    leaf was found (`requests` ordered before `limits`), and never copies `scaler`
    or any other peer key of the named resource block.
  @render_template (@render_template struct under the registered name
    `render_template`) takes `template`: @String and @data: @Value, constructs a
    brand-new @HandleBars::new() per call — the nested engine therefore sees all nine
    contextual helpers — and on any inner @vynil_core::Error logs @tracing::warn!
    and outputs the empty string; because the nested engine starts from a core-only
    base plus contextual helpers, any `{{> partial}}` or registered-template reference
    inside the nested text is unresolvable and always collapses to the empty string.
  @render_file takes `file`: @String and @data: @Value, reads the path through
    @std::fs::read_to_string resolved against the process working directory, renders
    it via @vynil_core::hbs::HandleBars::render_named — which registers the template
    under the file-path name inside that fresh engine only — and likewise maps read,
    parse, and render failures to @tracing::warn! plus empty-string output; file text
    with no `{{ }}` tokens passes through byte-for-byte including its trailing newline,
    and nothing caps a template that calls `render_file` on itself.
  The Rhai `render_named` bridge (the last method of @handlebars_rhai_register) is
    the core @vynil_core::hbs::HandleBars::rhai_render_named: it registers the template
    in the
    live engine instead of a throwaway one, so the name persists for the rest of that
    engine — a later `{{> name}}` partial reference in the same engine renders the
    leaked template, and a repeated call with the same name silently overwrites it.
  @handlebars_rhai_register adds to the passed @rhai::Engine exactly
    @rhai::Engine::register_type_with_name under the script type name `"HandleBars"`
    and five global functions — `new_hbs` (@HandleBars::new, per call), and the
    methods `register_template`
    (@name @String, @template @String → @crate::RhaiRes<@rhai::Dynamic> unit),
    `register_partial_dir` (@directory @String), `register_helper_dir`
    (@directory @String), `render_from` (@template @String, @data @rhai::Map →
    @crate::RhaiRes<@String>) and `render_named` (@name @String, @template @String,
    @data @rhai::Map → @crate::RhaiRes<@String>) dispatched to
    @vynil_core::hbs::HandleBars::rhai_register_template,
    @vynil_core::hbs::HandleBars::rhai_register_partial_dir,
    @vynil_core::hbs::HandleBars::rhai_register_helper_dir,
    @vynil_core::hbs::HandleBars::rhai_render and
    @vynil_core::hbs::HandleBars::rhai_render_named through @std::ops::DerefMut;
    directory arguments naming a missing or non-directory path are accepted with no
    effect, and both dir methods load only their suffix — `*.rhai` files as script
    helpers named after the basename, `*.hbs` files as templates — core-side behavior.
  @is_native_hbs_helper answers pure literal membership of @name: it is `true` exactly
    when @name is in @vynil_core::hbs::CORE_HBS_HELPERS or in @VYNIL_HBS_HELPERS,
    consulting no engine — `inline` is answered native although that name is
    registered as a decorator and a helper lookup fails, and names gated out of the
    build by Cargo features would still answer native.
  The nine registered names are disjoint from the handlebars `6.4.2` built-in helper
    set (`if`, `unless`, `each`, `with`, `lookup`, `raw`, `log`, `eq`, `ne`, `gt`,
    `gte`, `lt`, `lte`, `and`, `or`, `not`, `len`, the case helpers) and from the
    misc/core helper surface, so @HandleBars::new registers nothing over anything a
    probe of the built engine can reach; conversely `helperMissing`,
    `blockHelperMissing` and `else` are `false` in @is_native_hbs_helper.
  Object key order follows the locked @serde_json `1.0.150` with `preserve_order`
    unified by the handlebars dependency: selector/labels output keeps the context
    order with the `comp` key last, and `resources_from_ctx` emits `requests` before
    `limits`.
  @HandleBars exposes its core: the tuple field is `pub` and @std::ops::Deref /
    @std::ops::DerefMut target @vynil_core::hbs::HandleBars, so Rust callers hold the
    whole core surface (@vynil_core::hbs::HandleBars::engine_mut,
    @vynil_core::hbs::HandleBars::render, @vynil_core::hbs::HandleBars::render_named,
    @vynil_core::hbs::HandleBars::register_template, the two dir registrars and the
    @crate::RhaiRes methods) beyond what this file itself defines; @Clone and @Debug
    derive over the inner engine; @HandleBars::new returns the @HandleBars<'static>
    instantiation regardless of any borrow scope.
  The in-file @tests pin the post-core-extraction lockstep contract in both
    directions: core generic helpers (@gen_password, @gen_private_key, base64,
    @url_encode, @to_decimal, @concat, @header_basic) must still render through
    @HandleBars::new(), and `new_hbs` on a registered engine must produce the common
    contextual surface — the regression test re-renders a package-style context to keep
    install/crds/backup script paths from silently losing the contextual helpers.

Depends on:
  `handlebars` `6.2.0` requested in `/common/Cargo.toml`, `6.4.2` locked in
    `/Cargo.lock`, features `script_helper` and `string_helpers` —
    @handlebars::handlebars_helper typed-parameter conversion (a @Value param accepts
    any JSON, a @String param accepts only JSON strings via @serde_json::from_value,
    a `str` hash only JSON strings, hash defaults applying only to absent keys),
    @handlebars::RenderErrorReason argument texts, @JsonRender::render placeholders,
    @handlebars::Handlebars engine semantics (registration overwrite, registered
    templates usable as partials), @handlebars::no_escape, and the re-export sources
    @handlebars::Path and @handlebars::PathSeg and @handlebars::template::{@Parameter,
    @Template, @TemplateElement}.
  `vynil-core` `0.7.7` from crates.io (`/common/Cargo.toml`, requested features
    `k8s,oci,s3,fs,shell,password` on default `http,crypto,rhai,hbs,hbs-scripting`) —
    @vynil_core::hbs::HandleBars supplies the base engine,
    @vynil_core::hbs::CORE_HBS_HELPERS supplies the core half of @is_native_hbs_helper,
    and the `rhai_*` wrappers plus @handlebars_misc_helpers `0.17.0` setup supply the
    strict-mode / no-escape / error-text behavior frozen above;
    @vynil_core::Error::HbsRenderError `Renderer error: ` and
    @vynil_core::Error::HbsTemplateError `Registering template failed with error: `
    are the prefixes scripts and Rust callers see.
  `handlebars_misc_helpers` `0.17.0` locked (`/common/Cargo.toml` features
    `string,json,jsonnet,regex,uuid` unified over core's request) —
    `new_hbs`/`setup_handlebars` installs strict mode and @handlebars::no_escape and
    the first-level helper set the engine carries.
  `rhai` `1.20.0` requested, `1.25.1` locked (`/common/Cargo.toml`, features
    `sync`, `serde`, `internals`) — @rhai::Engine registration, @rhai::Map, @rhai::Dynamic,
    `params` array semantics for script helpers, and the @serde_json round-trip of a
    @rhai::Map performed by the core `rhai_render` / `rhai_render_named` boundary.
  @serde_json `1.0.150` — @Value as the helper data currency and re-export target,
    `preserve_order` key stability unified via handlebars.
  @tracing::warn — the only signal for @render_template / @render_file failures.
  @crate::RhaiRes in ./lib.rs — the @rhai::EvalAltResult result alias used by every
    @handlebars_rhai_register bridge closure.
  @std::fs::read_to_string — @render_file template reads.

Exposes:
  @VYNIL_HBS_HELPERS — `pub const VYNIL_HBS_HELPERS: &[&str]` holding exactly the
    nine registered names in order: `selector_from_ctx`, `labels_from_ctx`,
    `ctx_have_crd`, `have_system_service`, `have_tenant_service`, `image_from_ctx`,
    `resources_from_ctx`, `render_template`, `render_file`; documentation positions it
    as the addition over @vynil_core::hbs::CORE_HBS_HELPERS.
  @is_native_hbs_helper — `#[must_use] pub fn is_native_hbs_helper(name: &str) -> bool`;
    `true` for any name in @vynil_core::hbs::CORE_HBS_HELPERS or @VYNIL_HBS_HELPERS
    (const membership, engine not consulted).
  @HandleBars — `pub struct HandleBars<'a>(pub @vynil_core::hbs::HandleBars<'a>)` with
    `#[derive(Clone, Debug)]` over the inner engine; @std::ops::Deref and
    @std::ops::DerefMut to @vynil_core::hbs::HandleBars grant the full core surface;
    the `pub` field allows bypassing every layer.
  @HandleBars::new — `#[must_use] pub fn new() -> @HandleBars<'static>`; the exact
    helper surface is the `Must` registration entry (seven @handlebars_helper helpers
    plus `image_from_ctx` and `resources_from_ctx` script helpers).
  @handlebars_rhai_register — `pub fn handlebars_rhai_register(engine: &mut @rhai::Engine)`;
    script-visible surface exactly as the `Must` bridge entry: custom type
    `"HandleBars"`, constructor `new_hbs`, methods `register_template`,
    `register_partial_dir`, `register_helper_dir`, `render_from`, `render_named`.
  Re-exports — `pub use` of @handlebars::Path as @HbsPath, @handlebars::PathSeg,
    @handlebars::template::@Parameter, @handlebars::template::@Template,
    @handlebars::template::@TemplateElement, and @serde_json::@Value; template-AST
    inspection and JSON data flow through these instead of the upstream paths.

Accepts:
  @HandleBars::new accepts nothing; @is_native_hbs_helper accepts any `&str` and never
    fails; @handlebars_rhai_register accepts any mutable @rhai::Engine and re-applies
    its six registrations idempotently, overwriting same-name entries.
  Template data is any @Value context; the contextual helpers freeze this data
    contract on top of it: `instance.selector` / `instance.labels` objects of string
    labels, `instance.images.<name>` objects with `registry` and `repository` plus an
    optional non-`null` `tag`, `instance.package.app_version` as the image tag
    fallback, `instance.resources.<name>.requests|limits.{cpu,memory}` leaf values of
    any JSON type, `cluster.crds` an array of strings, `cluster.services[]` and
    `tenant.services[]` objects carrying a string `key`; every other shape degrades
    to empty/false/absent rather than rejecting.
  `render_template` accepts any template text (@String param — non-string first
    parameter is a type-mismatch error) and any @Value data; `render_file` accepts any
    path text, read at call time against the process working directory.
  The Rhai bridge `render_from` / `render_named` accept any @rhai::Map — the core
    boundary JSON-serializes it (integers, floats, bools, strings, arrays, nested maps;
    the unit `()` becomes JSON `null`) before the engine sees it, and a @rhai::Dynamic
    that @serde_json cannot serialize fails the call before rendering.
  Script helpers receive every provided parameter positionally in `params` without
    type checking; a path resolving to undefined arrives as the absent-value path the
    script must itself guard.

Returns:
  @HandleBars::new returns the fully registered @HandleBars<'static> engine;
    @is_native_hbs_helper returns @bool.
  @selector / @labels return a JSON object (possibly `{}`); @have_crd,
    @have_system_service, @have_tenant_service return booleans rendered `true` /
    `false`; `image_from_ctx` returns the `registry/repository:tag` string;
    `resources_from_ctx` returns a possibly-empty map; booleans and numbers returned
    or looked up by helpers render plainly, objects render `[object]` in expression
    position.
  Both nested-rendering helpers return @String — the rendered text or `""`.
  @handlebars_rhai_register returns nothing; the script methods return
    @crate::RhaiRes payloads: unit, unit, unit, rendered @String, rendered @String.

Raises:
  Through the Deref'd @vynil_core::hbs::HandleBars::render surface, helper argument
    failures arrive as @vynil_core::Error::HbsRenderError whose display wraps the
    position clause `Error rendering "<name or Unnamed template>" line <l>, col <c>:`
    around the handlebars reasons `Helper/Decorator <struct> param with name <p> required but not found`
    (absent parameter or strict-mode undefined variable),
    `... param with name name type mismatch for String` (@have_crd, the two service
    probes given non-string names; same class for @render_template / @render_file
    non-string first parameters), and `Helper/Decorator selector hash with name comp type mismatch for str`
    for a non-string or `null` explicit `comp` (hash defaults apply only to absent
    keys); unknown helper names raise `Helper not found <name>`.
  Script-helper runtime failures arrive prefixed for the dynamic boundary:
    `Cannot convert data to Rhai dynamic: <rhai message> (line <l>, position <p>)` —
    out-of-bounds `params`, `Function not found: contains ((), ...)` for unknown image
    names, `Indexer unavailable: () [string]` for missing image fallback paths.
  @render_template and @render_file raise nothing outward — every inner failure
    (missing file, unparseable text, failed render) is @tracing::warn!-logged and
    returned as the empty string.
  The Rhai-registered methods raise @rhai::EvalAltResult errors on the script side:
    template-registration failures carry the @vynil_core::Error display prefix
    `Registering template failed with error: `, `render_from` / `render_named` render
    failures carry the bare handlebars text (`Error rendering ... Partial not found <p>`
    etc. plus the Rhai `Runtime error: ... (line <l>, position <p>)` wrap), and a
    non-serializable @rhai::Map fails with the @serde_json message — the
    registration-vs-render text asymmetry is the core wrappers'.
  No path in this file panics on reachable input: @Option::unwrap_or_default,
    @Option::is_some_and and @str::is_empty guard every fallible step, and the file
    contains no `unwrap()` / `expect()` calls; strict-mode and script failures are values.

Handles:
  Missing `comp` hash, empty `comp` string, absent or non-object `ctx`/`instance` —
    selector/labels answer `{}`, with `comp` inserted only when non-empty and
    component-key override keeping the original position.
  `tag` absent or explicit `null` in an image entry — the tag falls back to
    `instance.package.app_version`; unknown image name or missing `package` — hard
    render error (see Raises).
  Non-array `cluster.crds` / non-object service entries / non-string crds items —
    probes answer `false` instead of erroring.
  Undefined context paths reaching script helpers — `resources_from_ctx` null-chains
    to `{}`; `image_from_ctx` has no chain and errors.
  `render_file` on a missing, unparseable, or partial-referencing file, and
    `render_template` on a missing-partial template — @tracing::warn! then `""`.
  `register_partial_dir` / `register_helper_dir` naming a missing or non-directory
    path — accepted unchanged as a no-op (core `is_dir` gate).
  Registered-name reuse — @handlebars::Handlebars::register_helper overwrites any
    previous same-name helper of whichever layer it shadows, silently.

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover the contextual helper argument surface with in-file tests: selector/labels
      `comp` insert/override/no-op/non-object, `ctx_have_crd` string-equality plus the
      number-vs-string rejection, and the two service probes over mixed object/scalar
      arrays — none of the five has any mapped test today.
  [ ] Cover `image_from_ctx`: tag present, absent and `null` fallback to
      `package.app_version`, the `registry/repository:tag` shape, and the error texts
      for unknown name, missing `package`, and missing parameters. No mapped test exists.
  [ ] Cover `render_template` nested rendering: simple template with data,
      contextual helpers available in the nested engine, and missing-partial collapse
      to `""` with the warn swallowed. No mapped test exists.
  [ ] Cover `render_file`: existing template with trailing newline pass-through,
      read-error / unparseable-template / unresolvable-partial all landing at `""`.
      No mapped test exists.
  [ ] Cover strict-mode argument failures verbatim: absent ctx, undefined variable as
      the @Value/@String parameter, numeric `name`, and `comp=5`, asserting the exact
      `Helper/Decorator ...` texts including the macro-struct-name drift. No mapped
      test exists.
  [ ] Cover the no-HTML-escaping property and the `[object]` placeholder directly —
      @test_helper_url_encode currently accepts either `%26` or `&amp;`, so the engine
      escape contract could invert unnoticed.
  [ ] Cover the shared-engine leak of the Rhai `render_named` method: register under a
      name once, later render `{{> name}}` in the same engine, and repeat-name
      overwrite. No mapped test exists.
  [ ] Assert @VYNIL_HBS_HELPERS against the runtime engine and cover @is_native_hbs_helper
      `true`/`false` edges (`inline` as decorator, `helperMissing`, core names), so the
      const cannot drift from the registered surface silently.
  [?] `let _` discards the compile errors of @handlebars::Handlebars::register_script_helper
      — a future edit breaking either script leaves `image_from_ctx` /
      `resources_from_ctx` silently
      unregistered until something renders them. Decide later whether registration
      failures must fail engine construction.
  [?] @is_native_hbs_helper is const-membership, not engine truth: it answers native
      for `inline` (decorator only — a helper lookup fails) and would answer native
      for feature-gated core names in a leaner build. Decide later whether the gate
      becomes engine-driven or the list is corrected and feature-pinned.
  [?] Argument-error texts name the macro structs (`selector`, `labels`, `have_crd`)
      while templates call the registered aliases (`selector_from_ctx`,
      `labels_from_ctx`, `ctx_have_crd`) — one failure is hard to grep from the other.
      Decide later whether the struct names realign.
  [?] Helper objects print the literal `[object]` in expression position, so
      `{{selector_from_ctx this}}` silently produces junk text instead of JSON; only
      subexpression/block use works. Decide later whether the helpers should return
      rendered-JSON strings or the Value behavior stays documented.
  [?] @render_template / @render_file map every nested failure to the empty string plus
      @tracing::warn!: package scripts cannot distinguish empty output from broken
      templates, and the fresh nested engine can never see partials or templates
      registered by the outer render, so `{{> }}` inside these calls always collapses.
      Decide later whether errors must surface or partials be inherited.
  [?] `render_file` reads its path against the process working directory (no template
      base dir) and nothing guards a template file calling `render_file` on itself —
      only `{{> }}` self-include is refused upstream, helper recursion is live
      recursion. Decide later whether path resolution and recursion depth need rules.
  [?] `image_from_ctx` is unguarded where `resources_from_ctx` null-chains: its
      failures surface as cryptic Rhai texts (`Function not found: contains ((), ...)`,
      `Indexer unavailable: ()`). Decide later whether it becomes a typed Rust helper
      or gains `?` guards.
  [?] Strict mode, the no-escape renderer, and the `[object]` behavior all belong to
      `handlebars_misc_helpers` `0.17.0` + `handlebars` `6.4.2` internals, not to this
      file, yet every claim here leans on them; a dependency bump could re-enable
      HTML escaping or soften strictness with no change in this file. Decide later
      whether @HandleBars::new re-asserts both settings itself.
  [?] The Rhai `render_named` bridge registers into the live shared engine (persistent
      partials, silent same-name overwrite, cross-render state) while `render_from`
      is clean — two persistence classes under one object. Decide later whether
      `render_named` should render without registering, as core's plain method could.
  [?] @Clone on @HandleBars clones the whole registered engine including script ASTs
      and leaked templates; no in-file rule says whether clones are meant to be cheap
      per-render or long-lived shared renderers. Confirm the intended ownership before
      consumers are reviewed.

Done when:
  Every Scenario above has a passing in-file test (or the gap is explicitly carried),
    the Tasks coverage checks are closed, and `cargo test -p common` with
    `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` are green.

Example:
  selector wire probe: `{{json_to_str (selector_from_ctx this comp="c1")}}` over
    `{"instance":{"selector":{"app":"z","tier":"w"}}}` yields
    `{"app":"z","tier":"w","app.kubernetes.io/component":"c1"}` — comp appended last
  direct-object wire: `{{selector_from_ctx this}}` yields the placeholder `[object]`
  argument error wire: `{{selector_from_ctx}}` yields `Renderer error: Error rendering "Unnamed template" line 1, col 1: Helper/Decorator selector param with name ctx required but not found`
  script-error wire: `{{image_from_ctx this "nope"}}` yields `Renderer error: Error rendering "Unnamed template" line 1, col 1: Cannot convert data to Rhai dynamic: Function not found: contains ((), &str | ImmutableString | String) (line 3, position 21)`
  image wires: with tag → `reg/repo/web:1.2`, tag absent or `null` →
    `reg/repo/web:9.9` from `package.app_version`

Scenario: Script map data reaches helpers as JSON
  Given a @rhai::Engine built by @handlebars_rhai_register and a script-built
    `#{}` map holding an @i64, a string, and a boolean
  When the script calls `new_hbs().render_from(...)` with it
  Then each value renders in its JSON form (`42`, `hello`, `true`) through the
    contextual engine
  Maps to test @test_rhai_render_scalar_values

Scenario: Nested script maps keep their shape
  Given a @rhai::Map with an inner map (`host`, `port`)
  When `render_from` renders a `{{svc.host}}:{{svc.port}}`-style path access
  Then nested path resolution succeeds against the JSON-converted map
  Maps to test @test_rhai_render_nested_map

Scenario: Script render_named renders with its data and registers its name
  Given a script calling `render_named("t", "result: {{v}}", #{v: "ok"})`
  Then the call returns `result: ok`
  And the same engine later renders `{{> t}}` with the leaked template instead of
    failing with a missing partial
  Maps to test @test_rhai_render_named_basic for the render leg; the persistence leg
    has no mapped test.

Scenario: Context selects and labels carry the component tag
  Given a context with `instance.selector` and `instance.labels` objects
  When `{{#each (selector_from_ctx this)}}` renders with and without `comp="c1"`, and
    `comp` is also given as an empty string or over an absent `instance`
  Then entries render in context order, `app.kubernetes.io/component` appears only
    for a non-empty `comp`, an existing component key is overwritten in place, and a
    context without the branch yields nothing to iterate
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: CRD and service probes answer from the cluster context
  Given contexts mixing a matching `crds` string, a number crds entry, object service
    entries with `key`, a bare string service entry, and a tenant-side twin
  When @ctx_have_crd, @have_system_service and @have_tenant_service render
  Then string matches answer `true`, type-mismatched entries never match, scalar
    service elements are skipped, and absent branches answer `false`
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Image reference falls back to the package app version
  Given `instance.images.web` with `registry` and `repository`, with `tag` present,
    absent, and `null`, plus `instance.package.app_version` as the fallback
  When `{{image_from_ctx this "web"}}` renders each context
  Then the presence of a non-`()` tag wins and both fallback shapes render
    `<registry>/<repository>:9.9`
  But an unknown image name or missing `package` aborts the render with the script
    error texts from Raises
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Resources extraction keeps only the k8s leaf keys
  Given `instance.resources.app` variants — full, requests-only, requests plus
    `scaler`, and an empty `instance`
  When `{{json_to_str (resources_from_ctx this "app")}}` renders each
  Then the four k8s leaf keys pass through with types, a parent key appears only with
    a leaf, `scaler` is never copied, and an empty context yields `{}`
  Maps to tests @test_resources_from_ctx_full_config,
    @test_resources_from_ctx_requests_only_no_limits_key,
    @test_resources_from_ctx_scaler_does_not_leak and
    @test_resources_from_ctx_empty_context_returns_empty_object

Scenario: Script-visible engine is the contextual engine
  Given a registered script building `#{ instance: #{ selector: ... } }` and calling
    `new_hbs()`
  When it renders `{{#each (selector_from_ctx this)}}{{@key}}={{this}}{{/each}}`
  Then the new engine exposes the contextual helpers — `app=demo` renders, proving
    `new_hbs` returns this file's engine and not the core-only one
  Maps to test @test_new_hbs_rhai_exposes_contextual_helpers

Scenario: Core generic surface survives into this engine
  Given template expressions for `gen_password` (length and `symbols=0`),
    `gen_private_key`
    (`ed25519`, `rsa bits=2048` PEM-parsed), `base64_encode` / `base64_decode`
    round-trip, `url_encode`, `to_decimal` (octal `755` and `0`), `concat`, and
    `header_basic`
  When each renders through @HandleBars::new()
  Then the core helper results are unchanged by this layer
  Maps to tests @test_helper_gen_password_length_and_classes,
    @test_helper_gen_password_symbols_disabled, @test_helper_gen_private_key_ed25519,
    @test_helper_gen_private_key_rsa_with_bits, @test_helper_base64_encode,
    @test_helper_base64_decode, @test_helper_base64_roundtrip,
    @test_helper_url_encode, @test_helper_to_decimal_octal,
    @test_helper_to_decimal_zero, @test_helper_concat and @test_helper_header_basic

Scenario: Nested render_template renders inline and collapses failures
  Given a template calling `{{render_template "Hi {{name}}" this}}` and another
    calling it with `{{> nope}}` inside
  When both render
  Then the inline template renders with the passed data while the inner missing
    partial — every partial reference does, in fact — yields the empty string plus a
    warning, never an outer error
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Files render through render_file and fail silently
  Given `render_file` calls naming a readable template file, a missing path, and an
    unparseable file
  When all three render
  Then the readable file renders with its trailing newline intact while the other two
    return the empty string after warnings
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Strict mode turns missing args into render errors
  Given calls missing the `ctx` parameter, passing an undefined variable as @ctx or
    as `name`, passing a number as `name`, and passing `comp=5`
  When any renders through the Deref'd core render surface
  Then each fails with the exact `Helper/Decorator <struct> param with name <p> required but not found`
    / `type mismatch` family named in Raises — errors name
    the macro structs, and the script helpers with no missing-`comp`-style
    requirement keep answering
  No mapped test exists.
